.TH SAFE-POWER 1 "2026-01-06" "safe-power 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
safe-power \- safely reboot or shut down a Linux system running Docker workloads
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B safe-power
.RB [ reboot | shutdown ]
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B safe-power
is a system-grade command-line utility designed to safely reboot or shut down a Linux host running Docker workloads.

Before initiating a reboot or power-off,
.B safe-power
ensures that running Docker containers are stopped cleanly. It integrates with
.BR systemd-inhibit (1)
to prevent shutdown/reboot from completing until container cleanup has finished, reducing race conditions and the risk of data corruption.

All actions are logged to journald using
.BR logger (1)
under the tag
.BR safe-power .
.SH ACTIONS
.TP
.B reboot
Reboot the system after stopping Docker containers.
.TP
.B shutdown
Power off the system after stopping Docker containers.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR --dryrun
Display the actions that would be performed without executing them. No reboot/shutdown occurs.
.TP
.BR --force
Skip Docker container shutdown entirely and immediately reboot or shut down.
.TP
.BI --timeout= N
Specify the timeout in seconds passed to
.BR docker\ stop .
Default is 20 seconds.
.TP
.BR --no-color
Disable ANSI color output.
.TP
.BR --noconfirm
Skip the interactive confirmation prompt.
.TP
.BR --verbose
Enable human-readable output (additional informational messages).
.TP
.BR --version
Print the program version and exit.
.SH LOGGING
All events are logged to journald under the tag
.BR safe-power .

Examples:
.PP
.nf
journalctl -t safe-power
journalctl -t safe-power -b
.fi
.SH SYSTEMD INHIBITOR LOCK
.B safe-power
uses
.B systemd-inhibit --mode=block
to prevent shutdown or reboot from completing until the script exits.

This guarantees that Docker container cleanup is not interrupted by external shutdown triggers (for example, shutdown initiated from a desktop session or remote management).
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Successful execution (or successful dry-run).
.TP
.B 1
Invalid arguments, user cancellation, or execution error.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/local/bin/safe-power
Main executable.
.TP
.I /usr/local/share/man/man1/safe-power.1
Manual page source.
.SH COMPATIBILITY
Ubuntu Server 24.04 LTS, Raspberry Pi OS (Debian-based), and other systemd-based Linux distributions.
.SH AUTHOR
Thomas
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR docker (1),
.BR systemd-inhibit (1),
.BR journalctl (1),
.BR reboot (8),
.BR poweroff (8)
